  "id": "doseresponse-relationship",
  "term": "dose–response relationship",
  "definition": "A dose–response relationship is the pattern linking how much of an intervention is given, such as its intensity, frequency, or duration, with the size or nature of its effects. In this context, it refers to how different amounts of exercise may relate to changes in sleep quality in people with depression.",
